# Autonomous Mode

## Before the user leaves
Scope the full task, surface ALL foreseeable questions at once, confirm understanding of the answers.

For multi-phase or ambiguous scope: run Spec gate + `grill-protocol.mdc` (mini or full) on the scope summary **or** confirm the user already grilled / answered product questions. Record grill outcomes in `.scratch/grill-notes.md` or DECISION-LOG.

**Models while away** (Job table in `subagents.mdc`):

| Role | Model | How |
|---|---|---|
| **Implement / build** | **Grok** (`cursor-grok-4.5-high`) | Prefer parent is Grok. If parent is not Grok → **spawn** Grok for implementation (don’t block the leave-behind asking the user to switch). |
| **Phase / post-build review → fix** | **Fable** (`claude-fable-5-thinking-medium`) | **Always spawn** Fable for critique + one fix pass at phase gates. Never leave Grok to self-review alone. |
| **Go-live / trust-boundary** | Premier per Job table (Sol / Fable) | Unchanged hard gates |

## While away
- Decide ambiguous items and log every one to DECISION-LOG.md (format below).
- Commits per `git-discipline.mdc` (push each step so progress is visible remotely).
- **At each phase gate:** spawn **Fable** for review (and fix blockers once) before advancing. Go-live still uses full `review-protocol.mdc` Premier loops.
- **Gate discipline** per `workflow.mdc` — no next phase while a gate is incomplete.
- Maintain `.scratch/run-state.md` (protocol, phase, last_gate_passed, open_blocked, last_commit, next_action); update on every gate pass.
- **High-risk decisions** (data loss, security, breaking changes, business logic): log with status **BLOCKED**, commit + push the log, and do NOT proceed past that point.

## DECISION-LOG.md format
```
## [Date] [Short description]
**What I had to decide:** ...
**Options I considered:** ...
**What I chose:** ...
**Why:** ...
**Status:** DECIDED / BLOCKED
```

## Log rotation (keeps session-start reads cheap)
- DECISION-LOG.md is **newest-first**.
- When it grows past ~150 lines: move everything except open BLOCKED entries and the current phase's decisions to **DECISION-LOG-ARCHIVE.md** (append, never trim), and leave a one-line marker at the bottom of the live log: "Older entries: DECISION-LOG-ARCHIVE.md". The archive is reference material -- read it only when a specific old decision matters.
- Same pattern for any other always-read file that grows without bound (e.g. TESTING-STRATEGY.md): live file stays small, history goes to an `-ARCHIVE` twin.

## When the user returns
Summary: what was done, decisions made, what's pending. User reviews the log and approves or overrides.
